  "Duplicate content across two NEW files of this wave: the symmetric power-tail stable limit is proved both as thm:p15-w02c-p15-016-stable (this packet, limit-theorems-and-concentration-w02c-p15-016.tex:153-180) and as thm:p15-w02c-p15-015-power-tail-limit (packet w02c-p15-015, limit-theorems-and-concentration-w02c-p15-015.tex:247); Durrett's Levy attribution (p.152) is likewise reported in both. The lead should reconcile at routing.",
  "Guard G13 flags a 16-word copied-prose run in limit-theorems-and-concentration-w02c-p15-016.tex; the run is the quoted, attributed Durrett phrase at lines 46-48 ('a reference that contains the last word on many results about sums of independent random variables').",
  "central-limit-theorems.tex:555-557 labels the Heyde/rate remark and the stable-law continuation as 'separate presentations' instead of stating them; this is the C030 gap.",
  "Source framing remarks in Durrett Section 3.4 not on the routed CLT chapter (chi notation chosen because the square of a normal is chi-squared, p.144; the roulette wheel layout, p.145; why the histogram correction treats {S>=11} as {S>=10.5}, p.146; pairwise independence suffices for the SLLN, p.147; why the truncation level c_n is chosen, p.151; exp(e^4)=5.15e23 scale remark, p.153) are judged framing rather than definitions/arguments/boundaries of C001/C005/C006/C019/C025; they are written in the unrouted file of packet w02c-p15-015.",
  "weak-laws-and-triangular-arrays annex refers to proved results without \\cref: 'The bounded fourth-moment lemma' (line 258; thm:p15-bounded-fourth-moment in independent-random-series.tex:97), 'The power-tail identity' (line 398; thm:p15-power-tail-tools in strong-law-rates-and-normalization.tex:41), 'Feller's already proved theorem' (line 563). The results exist earlier on the route.",
